Subject: [PATCH] minimum arm64: ship curl, grep, gzip, less, sed, tar and wget

A fresh RENKU arm64 guest had no way to fetch or unpack anything except
pkgman: no curl, wget, tar, gzip, grep or sed, no python, and a bash built
without /dev/tcp. grep, less and sed come from the HaikuPorts arm64
bootstrap packages the build already downloads. curl (OpenSSL), wget
(OpenSSL), tar and gzip are not on HaikuPorts for arm64; they are
cross-built by pkgman-repo's scripts/cross-arm64-cli.sh, published in RENKU
Apps, and listed here under their own names like zstd in 0009. Their hpkgs
are in ../packages/, and add-media-arm64.sh copies them into the generated
directory's download/.

The bootstrap curl and curl_devel are dropped from the repository list: one
repository cannot hold two packages named curl ("package curl has already
been added!"), and nothing in the build uses curl_devel.

The copies in ../packages/ say vendor "Haiku Project": package_repo refuses
a package whose vendor differs from the repository's, and this is the
HaikuPorts build repository. The ones published in RENKU Apps say "RENKU"
for the same reason. Because the repository list changed, its checksum no
longer matches anything on Haiku's CDN; build with HAIKU_NO_DOWNLOADS=1 so
jam indexes download/ locally instead of fetching.

If @minimum-anyboot then fails with "failed to open ISO file", build
haiku-boot-cd.iso first (jam -q @minimum-anyboot haiku-boot-cd.iso): the
anyboot rule reads it but did not rebuild it after it went missing.

diff -ru a/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles b/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles
--- a/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles	2026-09-30 09:39:31.131886997 +0000
+++ b/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles	2026-09-30 09:39:31.132887281 +0000
@@ -191,6 +191,24 @@
 				ca_root_certificates
 				openssl3
 				;
+
+			# A fresh arm64 guest had no way to fetch or unpack anything but
+			# pkgman: no wget, tar, gzip, grep or sed, and bash without /dev/tcp.
+			# grep, less and sed are HaikuPorts bootstrap packages; wget, tar and
+			# gzip are cross-built (pkgman-repo scripts/cross-arm64-cli.sh), and
+			# so is curl, which needs the SOCK_NONBLOCK fix in 0013 or its own
+			# workaround (it has both).
+			if $(TARGET_PACKAGING_ARCH) = arm64 {
+				AddHaikuImageSystemPackages
+					curl
+					grep
+					gzip
+					less
+					sed
+					tar
+					wget
+					;
+			}
 		}
 
 		case "test-*" : {
diff -ru a/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64 b/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64
--- a/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64	2026-09-30 09:39:31.132887281 +0000
+++ b/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64	2026-09-30 09:39:31.133887565 +0000
@@ -15,8 +15,9 @@
 	binutils-2.41_2026_03_10_bootstrap-1
 	bison-3.8.2_bootstrap-1
 	coreutils-9.9_bootstrap-1
-	curl-8.19.0_bootstrap-1
-	curl_devel-8.19.0_bootstrap-1
+	# curl and curl_devel 8.19.0_bootstrap are replaced by the cross-built
+	# curl below (one repository cannot hold two packages named curl, and
+	# nothing in the build uses curl_devel).
 	expat-2.5.0_bootstrap-1
 	expat_devel-2.5.0_bootstrap-1
 	findutils-4.9.0_bootstrap-1
@@ -48,6 +49,12 @@
 	# zstd-compressed package, which is what every HaikuPorts package is.
 	zstd-1.5.6-2
 	zstd_devel-1.5.6-2
+	# Also not in HaikuPorts for arm64: cross-built by pkgman-repo's
+	# scripts/cross-arm64-cli.sh and published in RENKU Apps.
+	curl-8.22.0-2
+	gzip-1.13-1
+	tar-1.35-1
+	wget-1.24.5-1
 	:
 	# source packages
 	bash
